  "narration": {
    "title": "The Yankees Own the Mound, Top to Bottom",
    "intro": "It's a pitching day, and one team runs both charts. New York has the best rotation ERA in the game and the best bullpen ERA too, a rare double. Behind them, the arms keeping their clubs afloat and one lefty finally trending up.",
    "staff_lead": "The Yankees lead the rotation board at a 3.34 ERA with a 1.15 WHIP, with Detroit a step back at 3.50. Cam Schlittler is a big reason New York keeps the top spot, sitting at a 2.04 ERA and a form of 88.",
    "bullpen_lead": "New York holds the bullpen chart too, at 3.05, just ahead of Boston's 3.15. Atlanta and Milwaukee are knotted at 3.36 behind them.",
    "arms_lead": "Jacob Misiorowski still headlines at a 1.97 ERA and a 0.79 WHIP for Milwaukee, though his form slipped from 97 to 95 on the week. Dylan Cease owns the shiniest ERA of the group at 2.40 for Toronto, while Drew Rasmussen ticked up to a form of 80.",
    "risers_lead": "Jesus Luzardo is the one moving the right way, his form up four to 73. Not elite yet, but the arrow points up while Logan Webb (down six to 57) and Logan Gilbert (down five to 64) went the other way."
  }
